[127.124645, "o", "# Log Filter Bug Fix Summary\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n- 40% of ERROR logs from payment-svc were being dropped from errors.log\r\n- They were appearing in raw.log but not in output/errors.log\r\n- Other services (auth-service, inventory-service) were working fine\r\n\r\n## Root Cause\r\nThe `classify_line()` function in filter.py had a flawed detection logic:\r\n```python\r\nif 'T' in line[:25] and ':' in line[:25]:\r\n    return 'structured'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis was intended to detect structured/JSON logs, but it incorrectly matched:\r\n- Payment-svc logs: `2024-01-15T08:48:40+00:00 [ERROR] service=payment-svc ...`\r\n  (ISO 8601 timestamp with 'T' and ':' in first 25 chars)\r\n\r\nWhile NOT matching:\r\n- Auth/inventory logs: `[ERROR] 2024-01-15 08:30:16 service=auth-service ...`\r\n  (No 'T' in timestamp format)\r\n\r\nResult: Payment-svc ERROR logs were routed to structured.log instead of errors.log\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nSimplified classify_line() to only detect actual JSON:\r\n```python\r\ndef classify_line(line):\r\n    stripped = line.strip()\r\n    if stripped.star"]
[127.124662, "o", "tswith('{') and stripped.endswith('}'):\r\n        return 'structured'\r\n    return 'plaintext'\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n- Before fix: 76 payment-svc ERROR logs in raw.log, 0 in errors.log (in structured.log instead)\r\n- After fix: 76 payment-svc ERROR logs in raw.log, 76 in errors.log\r\n- Total ERROR logs: 127/127 correctly routed (100% capture rate)\r\n\r\n## Files Modified\r\n- filter.py (backed up to filter.py.bak)\r\n"]
